:: The Helpful Son [event mom_quest] {"position":"3150,700","size":"100,100"}
<<silent>><<SetBackground "images/locations/reception.jpg">><</silent>>
The glass doors slide apart before I'm even close to them, like the building has already decided I'm allowed in. Inside, LED strips run along the ceiling, and the marble floor throws their light back up so the whole lobby glows. There's a lounge corner with leather chairs nobody is sitting in and a coffee machine that probably costs more than my car. I try not to look impressed, and I'm pretty sure it doesn't work.

Behind the reception desk a young woman in a blazer is already smiling at me with professional patience.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs to [
    { who: "Receptionist", text: "Good morning, sir, welcome to AdvanTec. How can I help you?" },
    { who: $player, text: "Morning. I'm here to see my $mom.relation, $mom.name $mom.surname." },
    { who: "Receptionist", text: "Of course. Let me just check with Mr. $boss.surname first..." },
    { who: $player, text: "Oh, you really don't have to bother him. I'm just dropping off something she needs for their meeting this afternoon. Two minutes, tops." },
    { text: "Her hand hovers over the phone. I can see her picture it: calling $boss.callName's office to ask permission for a delivery. She takes her hand back." },
    { who: "Receptionist", text: "Well... all right. Make it quick, okay? Ms. $mom.surname is on the sixth floor." },
    { who: $player, text: "In and out. Thanks a lot." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

<<linkreplace "Take the elevator up">>
<<silently>><<SetBackground "images/locations/elevator.jpg">><</silently>>
One of the elevators is already waiting with its doors open, as if it's been expecting me too. Inside it's more marble and mirrors on three sides, so I get to watch several versions of myself press the button for the sixth floor. None of them look like they belong here. The doors close with a soft chime and the floor numbers start counting up.

<<linkreplace "Step out">>
<<silently>>
<<SetLocation "Moms Work">>
<<CheckLocation>>
<</silently>>
The sixth floor is one big open office, all keyboards and murmured phone calls and the occasional printer groaning in a corner. I spot $mom.callName near the windows, leaning toward her screen with her glasses pushed up into her hair. She doesn't notice me weaving through the desks. When I get close enough, I can read the mail she's writing, something very polite to a "Hugh Blackwell" that she's clearly rewritten three times.

<<Video "images/characters/mom/activities/working_1.mp4" "" "" 500>>

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs to [
    { who: $player, text: "Knock knock. Hope I'm not interrupting anything important." },
    { text: "She jumps a little, then turns, and her whole face changes when she sees it's me." },
    { who: $mom, text: "Honey! I thought you'd text me first. How did you even get up here?" },
    { who: $player, text: "I told the receptionist I had to bring you something for a meeting. She believed me." },
    { who: $mom, text: "Oh, $player.name. You and your little white lies." },
    { who: $player, text: "It's only half a lie. I did bring you something. The prototype, remember?" },
    { who: $mom, text: "Of course I remember, I've been thinking about it all morning. And today's actually been quieter than yesterday, mostly because he hasn't come out of his office yet, so knock on wood." },
    { who: $player, text: "Then let's use the quiet. Do you have a few minutes?" },
    { who: $mom, text: "Sure, just let me send this off to Mr. Blackwell and then we can..." },
    { text: "Across the room a door bangs open, hard enough that half the office looks up." },
    { who: $boss, text: "$mom.surname! Meeting room. Now." },
    { text: "She goes still. Her hand stays frozen over the mouse, and I watch the color drain out of her face in the time it takes him to turn around." },
    { who: $mom, text: "It's fine, it'll only take a minute, sweetie. Stay right here, okay? There's a granola bar in my top drawer if you get hungry." },
    { who: $player, text: "Sure. Good luck." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>
<<linkreplace "Watch her go">>
She smooths her skirt on the way, the way people straighten things when they can't straighten anything else. The glass door closes behind them. For about ten seconds it's quiet, and then he gets loud.

I can't make out the words through the glass, only the shape of them. He's jabbing a finger at a printout, then at her, then at the printout again. She's nodding. She keeps nodding.

<<Video "images/characters/mom/activities/working_2.mp4" "" "" 500>>

Around me, people very carefully keep typing. A guy two desks over puts his headphones on. Nobody looks at the meeting room for longer than a second, and nobody gets up. It goes on for more than ten minutes, and I watch every one of them.

I'm angry, but it's a quiet kind of angry, and mostly I just watch: how small she makes herself in that chair, how fast she agrees with whatever he says, how easily one man with a loud voice gets her to do what he wants. I don't love that I'm paying such close attention to that last part. I keep doing it anyway.

Eventually the door opens. He walks off toward his office without looking at anyone, and $mom.callName comes back to her desk, where I'm already waiting.

[[Talk to her|The Helpful Son 2]]
